<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bình Ngô đại cáo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1428</span> · Also known as Great Proclamation upon the Pacification of the Wu, Binh Ngo dai cao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bình Ngô đại cáo is a proclamation written in classical Chinese by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-trai">Nguyễn Trãi</a> in 1428 on behalf of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a> to announce victory over the Ming and the restoration of Đại Việt. Asserting that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> had its own territory, customs and dynasties equal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s, it is regarded as a classic declaration of Vietnamese independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/binh-ngo-dai-cao.jpg" alt="Bình Ngô đại cáo" width="320" height="346" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nguyễn Trãi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%ACnh_Ng%C3%B4_%C4%91%E1%BA%A1i_c%C3%A1o_%E5%B9%B3%E5%90%B3%E5%A4%A7%E8%AA%A5.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
